          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "13.3.3 Nitrogen cycle"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.222,
            0.111,
            0.89,
            0.214
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Nitrogen is an essential element for the synthesis of proteins and nucleic acids in all living organisms. The largest reservoir of nitrogen is in our atmosphere. However, nitrogen gas (N ) is rather non-reactive, and cannot be directly used by plants and animals. It must first be converted to soluble compounds that living beings can absorb. The overall movement of nitrogen between air, soil, water and organisms is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "nitrogen",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.056,
            0.219,
            0.476,
            0.485
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 2,
              "bbox": [
                0.056,
                0.219,
                0.476,
                0.485
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_12_image_2.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 3,
              "bbox": [
                0.192,
                0.491,
                0.378,
                0.508
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 13.15: Nitrogen cycle"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.487,
            0.213,
            0.89,
            0.281
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "cycle",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (Fig. 13.15). The nitrogen cycle contains several steps — nitrogen fixation, assimilation"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", ammonification",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "nitrification",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "denitrification",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ],
          "continues_prev": true
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.486,
            0.283,
            0.89,
            0.52
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Nitrogen-fixing bacteria, such as Rhizobium in the root nodules of legumes and Azotobacter in the soil, convert atmospheric "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { N } _ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " into ammonia (NH"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3",
              "styles": [
                "subscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "). Nitrifying bacteria like Nitrosomonas convert ammonia into nitrite (NO–2), while Nitrobacter convert nitrite into nitrate (NO–3). This process is known as "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "nitrification",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". Plants assimilate these nitrogen compounds from the soil, whereas animals obtain nitrogen by consuming plants or other animals. When plants and animals die or produce waste, decomposers like bacteria and fungi break the organic matter,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.222,
            0.519,
            0.891,
            0.621
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "returning nitrogen compounds like ammonia to the soil. This process is known as "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "ammonification",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". Denitrifying bacteria, such as Pseudomonas convert some nitrates back into nitrogen gas. This process is known as "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "denitrification",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". This completes the cycle and maintains a balance of nitrogen in ecosystems. Lightning also contributes to the fixation of nitrogen oxides."
            }
          ],
          "continues_prev": true
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.623,
            0.252,
            0.689
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.186,
                0.623,
                0.252,
                0.689
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_12_image_7.jpg",
